WEBVTT

00:04:50.572 --> 00:04:51.572
This has been it.

00:04:53.036 --> 00:04:55.036
Noah King

00:04:58.732 --> 00:04:59.572
This is Gordon.

00:05:02.844 --> 00:05:03.544
Are you in there?

00:05:05.788 --> 00:05:06.788
Miss Gordon?

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:15.640
See you at me.

00:05:35.212 --> 00:05:37.212
Thanks, everybody.

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:25.130
Somebody answered.

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:56.050
I'm not going to hurt you like it calm down

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:01.630
I am not going to hurt you.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:04.680
Why did you chase me?

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:07.200
Why did you run?

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:12.320
There was a girl on the street. I thought...

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:13.210
That I killed her?

00:10:13.390 --> 00:10:16.280
Look, it won't make you feel any better.

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:16.940
Think this over.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:19.560
If I had killed her, I'd be miles away from here by now, wouldn't I?

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:24.690
I suppose you're right.

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:29.980
It's just that the whole city's so quiet and empty, I...

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:31.970
Well, what could have happened?

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:33.710
I wish I knew.

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:39.020
Everything since dinner last night is a complete blank to me.

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:40.790
I don't understand.

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:44.240
Well, I only got here from Detroit yesterday afternoon.

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:47.180
Just killing time between trains.

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:51.080
I should have known better than to flash a big roll in a bar.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:52.860
You mean you were robbed?

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:56.070
Yeah, and slugged and dumped in an alley.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:10:59.960
Then you were unconscious through most of the night.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.060
Oh, I came to about noon.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:05.630
The only thing I had left was a headache.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:09.700
I owe you an apology.

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:12.740
That makes us even.

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:15.580
You know the way back to the center of town?

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:16.540
Yes.

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:18.320
We'd better get moving.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:24.820
Better chance of finding out what's happened when we get there.

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:29.970
Not that it's so...

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:37.700
important at a time like this but my name is frank brooks i'm i'm norah king hi hello how come

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:43.760
you're still in town i was asleep in my room and the door was locked well then you haven't any idea

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:49.640
what happened last night no have you well there's been an evacuation of some kind but the question

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:56.420
is why dh farm maybe there's going to be an attack possible but i don't think so the enemy

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:59.720
wouldn't give us advance notice of a thing like that what about our radar

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:03.260
Four or five hours warning at best.

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:06.800
It's taken at least twice that long to evacuate the city.

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:10.420
Well, then how about German warfare? There's been a lot of talk about that.

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:13.770
The water isn't running. As far as that goes, none of the utilities are working.

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:16.490
Well, in that case, there'd still be patrols around town.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:18.530
The army, the police, civilian defense.

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:22.600
Well, for some reason, they had to get everybody out of town.

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:24.930
But there were half a million people here yesterday.

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:27.600
Now, for all we know, there are just the two of us left.

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:29.700
Doesn't make sense.

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:34.580
It has to. It happened in about 12 hours, too.

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:37.420
I wonder if there's anyone else left in town.

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:39.290
Probably a few.

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:41.900
Ever try to empty a sack of sugar?

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:43.960
What's that got to do with it?

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:47.000
Some of the grains always stick to the sack, like the two of us.

00:12:48.470 --> 00:12:50.670
Something tells me we'd better get out of here fast.

00:12:50.890 --> 00:12:53.440
How would you like to go, bus or taxi?

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:54.710
I'm serious, Nora.

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:57.330
The only reason they'd clear out an entire city like this

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:58.830
would be to get away from certain death.

00:12:59.230 --> 00:12:59.970
That would mean anyone...

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:07.160
still here is a dead pigeon funny i was so anxious trying to find somebody anybody that i

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:14.880
never thought of that i did you don't seem to be worried at all maybe not not of dying anyway

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:20.350
dying is such a normal thing but nobody around we'd better start walking toward the center of town

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:24.020
we only knew how much time we have

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:10.660
She won't find anyone in there either.

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:12.160
I know, but I just had an idea.

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:14.440
If we could get our hands on a portable battery radio,

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:19.760
we might be able to take you back from it.

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:20.380
What are you going to do?

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:25.890
Stand back so you don't get cut by flying glass.

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:35.680
So far, so good.

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:38.960
You know, they shoot people for looting at times like this.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:41.220
I don't care, just so we find a radio that works.

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:43.880
I don't see any.

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:45.850
You check that display case.

00:14:45.970 --> 00:14:47.090
I'll see if there's anything back here.

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:47.870
Frank, look.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.200
I'm afraid you're wasting your time.

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:51.220
Phones are out, too.

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:52.460
I checked a couple of them earlier.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:07.440
i'm afraid not looks like you're not doing too well even oh we're not licked yet let's try the

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:15.770
back room oh this is more like it there must be at least one set in all this junk well ordinarily

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:19.970
i suppose there would be but portables would be at a premium at a time like this the army

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:22.050
probably ordered everyone who could to carry one

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:31.440
Turn it on quick.

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:36.350
Battery.

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:39.660
Probably ship them separately.

00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:41.000
There must be one somewhere.

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:44.820
It's no use, Nora. I've already checked that shelf.

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:47.150
There isn't a battery in the place.

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:48.840
We're right back where we started.

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:50.680
Well, at least we're still alive.

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:51.620
But for how long?

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:54.040
It's getting worse every minute, isn't it?

00:15:54.690 --> 00:15:55.590
Think we'd better get out of here.

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:57.130
We can't afford to waste any more time.

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:26.240
that be quiet and listen it's like a piano coming from up the street well let's take a look the whole

00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:29.820
town's deserted we might be blown up any minute and somebody's in there playing

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:40.380
piano as if they didn't even care. Yeah. Wait here while I check. You mean alone? But be quiet.

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:15.890
Oh, later, the world's gone dry.

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:21.440
If it joined us anyway, treat a lady like that.

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:25.230
Well, I'll be.

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:29.730
Bollinger, 43, or Bollinger, 48.

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:36.980
makes no difference just so it's wet right that's good enough views good enough let's have one of

00:17:36.980 --> 00:17:55.810
each gold times eh vicky are you kidding me when'd you ever buy me champagne i was saving it for our

00:17:55.810 --> 00:17:59.740
honeymoon oh gregor falls well

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:03.540
What do you know? After 10 years, I've finally made it.

00:18:06.290 --> 00:18:11.960
I understand. They're celebrating as though it were New Year's Eve.

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:13.710
Maybe they just like privacy.

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:16.730
They're crazy, or we are.

00:18:18.060 --> 00:18:19.980
One way to find out. Come on.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.350
What do you know? Hey, Vicki, we got guests.

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:29.360
What did I tell you? We weren't the only ones left behind.

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:29.980
Come on!

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.400
Come on, sit down. Join the party.

00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:33.170
Hey, what are you two doing here?

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:35.740
Waiter, glasses please.

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:36.700
Very good, madam.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:39.080
Oh, now look, the whole city's deserted.

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:40.800
We've been all over town looking for someone.

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:42.080
What are you doing here?

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:44.660
Living, man. Really living.

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:48.670
Hey, you ain't the guy that owns this dump, are you?

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:50.490
No. Hardly. I'm Nora King.

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:51.950
This is Frank Brooks from Detroit.

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:56.810
Detroit, huh? You sure picked a fine time to visit this town.

00:18:56.950 --> 00:18:58.190
You can say that again.

00:18:58.190 --> 00:18:59.980
You sure picked a fi-

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:02.240
All right, we heard you the first time.

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:04.440
That's Vicki Harris. Never shuts up.

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:05.560
I'm Jim Wilson.

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:07.860
Well, now that we're all friends, how about some champagne?

00:19:08.020 --> 00:19:10.080
You mean you're going to sit here and whoop it up

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:12.360
when heaven knows what's going to happen or when?

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:13.980
Not just here, lady.

00:19:14.260 --> 00:19:16.780
There are a lot of high-class joints who always wanted to crash.

00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:19.310
The St. Regis, the Ritz, we're going to hit them all.

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:22.250
That's what you said last night. Now look at the spot we're in.

00:19:22.980 --> 00:19:25.750
Hey, honey, you look like you could stand something to eat.

00:19:25.950 --> 00:19:27.730
At a time like this, no thanks.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:29.970
Now, wait a minute, Nora. She's right. We'd better have something.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.700
while we figure out what to do next.

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:35.220
Well, there's everything in the joint from roast turkey to salami.

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:36.840
I'll see what I can whip up.

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:39.500
Uh, doll face. Fill her up.

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:43.180
I said I wanted a drink, not a bath.

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:47.120
How about a little more turkey?

00:19:47.380 --> 00:19:50.540
Mmm, not me. One more bite and I'd split my girdle.

00:19:50.760 --> 00:19:51.760
I know just what you mean.

00:19:52.310 --> 00:19:53.790
You know, there's no telling how long it'll be

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:55.890
before we run across any more food like this.

00:19:56.030 --> 00:19:57.850
We ought to try to figure out a way to take some with us.

00:19:58.310 --> 00:19:59.530
What makes you think you're going anywhere?

00:20:00.350 --> 00:20:02.450
Well, use your head. You can't stay here indefinitely.

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:04.180
Why not? We're doing all right.

00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:06.860
Yeah, maybe, but our luck can't hold out forever.

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:08.580
We should at least try to get out of town.

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:11.260
What? And leave all this? Not on your life.

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:13.100
We never had it so good, right, Vicki?

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:15.980
Right. I spoiled the party.

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:19.120
First decent joint you've taken me to in ten years.

00:20:19.810 --> 00:20:21.110
That's only because it's free.

00:20:22.350 --> 00:20:22.930
Fill her up.

00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:34.850
You know, this isn't the only good nightclub in town.

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:37.240
Why don't we try the, uh, Club Royale?

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:39.200
Now you're talking.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:42.070
What? That's over five miles away on the main highway.

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:45.390
Well, whatever. There ought to be plenty of places along the way we can stop.

00:20:45.570 --> 00:20:48.210
And who knows, we may even find a portable radio while we're at it.

00:20:49.990 --> 00:20:51.270
Well, if you put it like that.

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:57.290
Okay, let's go.

00:21:00.060 --> 00:21:29.860
sure you can make it? Are you kidding? Come on, honey. I'm with you. Well, swing low, sweet

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:33.160
Just when my feet were beginning to kill me.

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:34.320
Be my guest.

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:43.810
Hey, just like the girl in the alley.

00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:45.960
I think I'm gonna be sick.

00:21:46.930 --> 00:21:47.950
Better give Vicki a hand.

00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:50.530
How do you think it happened?

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:52.410
I wish I knew.

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:54.870
Keys are still in ignition.

00:21:55.830 --> 00:21:56.750
I hope you can get them out of the way.

00:22:03.200 --> 00:22:04.400
Let's see if we can get this thing started.

00:22:14.430 --> 00:22:15.770
He's probably dead.

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:17.180
Battery must be dead.

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:18.520
The radio doesn't work either.

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:20.340
Let's have a look under the hood.

00:22:26.080 --> 00:22:27.200
It's like somebody beat us to it.

00:22:27.580 --> 00:22:29.560
Let's hope I'm a better mechanic than he was.

00:22:36.270 --> 00:22:36.850
What's wrong?

00:22:40.680 --> 00:22:42.660
Distributor cap is off and the arm is missing.

00:22:43.310 --> 00:22:44.710
What does that mean in English?

00:22:45.030 --> 00:22:46.590
It means you can't get the engine started.

00:22:46.910 --> 00:22:50.390
Who are you?

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:51.700
Otis is the name.

00:22:51.900 --> 00:22:52.660
Charles Otis.

00:22:53.620 --> 00:22:54.780
I hope I didn't frighten you.

00:22:55.640 --> 00:22:56.100
Oh, no.

00:22:56.410 --> 00:22:57.990
I always shake like this.

00:22:58.320 --> 00:22:59.080
What are you doing here?

00:22:59.720 --> 00:22:59.960
Trying to...

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:04.650
get out of town like yourselves only won't do any good to look for a car in running condition

00:23:04.650 --> 00:23:09.580
what makes you so sure of that i tried a half a dozen in the last three or four miles the

00:23:10.310 --> 00:23:15.560
distributor arms are missing and all of them who are you trying to kid not so fast jim seems to

00:23:15.560 --> 00:23:19.180
me they did something like this in england during the war when they thought they'd be invaded did

00:23:19.180 --> 00:23:23.140
what ordered the distributor caps removed whenever a car was left unattended but that

00:23:23.140 --> 00:23:27.140
still doesn't explain why he was killed well here's one gal that's not going to hang around

00:23:27.140 --> 00:23:29.720
wondering even if i have to walk clear out of this state

00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:31.080
Which way did you come?

00:23:31.460 --> 00:23:33.060
From the north, uptown.

00:23:33.610 --> 00:23:34.450
You'd never believe it.

00:23:34.880 --> 00:23:35.840
The whole town's a wreck.

00:23:36.540 --> 00:23:37.400
Windows smashed.

00:23:37.700 --> 00:23:39.240
Houses and stores wrecked.

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:42.090
There must have been a lot of looting before everyone cleared out.

00:23:42.820 --> 00:23:43.440
I figure, sir.

00:23:44.140 --> 00:23:45.020
Did you see any people?

00:23:45.750 --> 00:23:47.960
About a dozen, like that.

00:23:49.110 --> 00:23:50.790
They all seemed to be killed the same way.

00:23:51.780 --> 00:23:54.470
There was one guy just outside an art store.

00:23:55.140 --> 00:23:58.730
Must have been trying to get away with the painting when they got him.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.000
That means they're already in the north end of town.

00:24:02.620 --> 00:24:04.620
and in the west, near my rooming house.

00:24:04.988 --> 00:24:05.988
Frank, I'm scared.

00:24:06.492 --> 00:24:07.532
You're not the only one.

00:24:15.388 --> 00:24:16.388
get me out of here.

00:24:16.604 --> 00:24:18.844
Don't be a fool. If you run out there, he'll spot us all.

00:24:18.944 --> 00:24:19.684
What do we do?

00:24:19.984 --> 00:24:21.184
Back against the wall. Quick!

00:24:27.292 --> 00:24:28.632
He can't see us from where he is.

00:24:33.036 --> 00:24:33.836
Doesn't look human.

00:24:34.412 --> 00:24:35.712
Don't let the shadow fool you.

00:24:36.012 --> 00:24:36.892
What else could it be?

00:24:37.420 --> 00:24:38.220
I wish I knew.

00:24:44.876 --> 00:24:45.876
Keep going away.

00:24:46.252 --> 00:24:47.552
Yeah, for how long?

00:24:47.884 --> 00:24:50.664
We can't stay here. We'll be killed, like all the others.

00:24:50.744 --> 00:24:52.104
Shut your mouth or I'll shut it for you.

00:24:53.900 --> 00:24:54.900
That hotel over there.

00:24:55.788 --> 00:24:57.168
Ought to be easy enough to get inside.

00:24:57.804 --> 00:24:59.184
Yeah, for us or for them?

00:24:59.596 --> 00:24:59.916
both.

00:25:00.250 --> 00:25:03.170
We have to make a break for it and hope we make it before they spot us.

00:25:03.250 --> 00:25:04.050
Then let's get started.

00:25:04.170 --> 00:25:06.250
Anything's better than standing out in the open like this.

00:25:06.680 --> 00:25:07.360
I'll go ahead.

00:25:07.560 --> 00:25:09.310
And if the coast is clear, I'll wave.

00:25:09.710 --> 00:25:10.720
What if it isn't?

00:25:11.050 --> 00:25:12.790
Then you can be the next guinea pig.

00:25:13.050 --> 00:25:14.530
Be careful.

00:25:16.080 --> 00:25:20.040
worry the street's probably a lot safer now than it is when the traffic is normal

00:26:06.620 --> 00:26:07.720
Do you think they spotted us?

00:26:08.580 --> 00:26:09.080
We'll know.

00:26:09.770 --> 00:26:10.210
Soon enough.

00:26:12.480 --> 00:26:13.890
Hey, Jim, do you see anything?

00:26:19.430 --> 00:26:20.710
Sign up, and the street's deserted.

00:26:21.030 --> 00:26:22.710
Aren't you the optimistic soul?

00:26:24.330 --> 00:26:24.590
Come on.

00:26:30.800 --> 00:26:31.280
What do we do now?

00:26:31.400 --> 00:26:33.880
We have to figure a way out of this.

00:26:34.260 --> 00:26:35.280
It's not going to be easy.

00:26:35.340 --> 00:26:36.520
We don't even know what we're up against.

00:26:38.720 --> 00:26:39.500
Take a look at this.

00:26:48.740 --> 00:26:57.860
State of national emergency was declared yesterday when hostile forces of unknown origin landed in open country approximately 50 miles due north of the city at 11 o'clock last night.

00:26:58.000 --> 00:26:59.750
While little is known as to strengthen.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:03.980
deployment of the enemy at this time, Bruce K. Peterson, in charge of civil defense for this

00:27:03.980 --> 00:27:09.960
area, ordered immediate evacuation of the city. I knew it was bad, but this... I don't believe it.

00:27:10.160 --> 00:27:15.600
Mystery man. Who are they kidding? Shadow on the wall. He could... I mean, they could be anywhere.

00:27:16.190 --> 00:27:21.190
Thousands of them. I don't think so. At least not yet. If they operate like we did during the last

00:27:21.190 --> 00:27:25.500
war, the one who almost spotted us was part of an advanced patrol. Then the rest won't be far

00:27:25.500 --> 00:27:29.890
behind. We're trapped. Right in the middle. They'll kill us all, I tell you. Take it easy.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:32.750
You've got plenty of trouble without you blowing your top.

00:27:32.930 --> 00:27:34.010
What do you expect me to do?

00:27:34.110 --> 00:27:36.630
Stand still while you sound off on military tactics?

00:27:37.040 --> 00:27:38.080
You got any better ideas?

00:27:38.860 --> 00:27:40.020
You bet I have.

00:27:40.240 --> 00:27:41.360
I'm getting out of here.

00:27:41.460 --> 00:27:41.760
Now.

00:27:42.040 --> 00:27:43.300
You're doing nothing of the kind.

00:27:43.520 --> 00:27:44.860
I'm warning you.

00:27:45.250 --> 00:27:46.730
Don't you try to stop me.

00:27:46.890 --> 00:27:48.740
But you can't go. It's suicide.

00:27:49.180 --> 00:27:50.920
They'll spot you before you've gone 50 feet.

00:27:51.120 --> 00:27:51.960
I'll take my chances.

00:27:52.180 --> 00:27:54.000
It'll be a lot easier getting past a few of them

00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:56.020
than waiting here for the whole army to show up.

00:27:56.080 --> 00:27:56.720
Wait a minute.

00:28:55.180 --> 00:28:56.320
He hasn't seen the rest of us.

00:28:57.660 --> 00:28:58.480
You'd better off upstairs.

00:28:58.720 --> 00:28:59.860
Chances are they won't take time.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:04.210
search all the buildings. Look, get over there by the stairs. I'll grab some keys from the desk.

00:29:04.350 --> 00:29:16.860
Come on, let's go. 402 to 404. Must be a sweep.

00:29:17.100 --> 00:29:17.360
Go ahead.

00:29:40.590 --> 00:29:41.170
Take yourself home.

00:29:41.720 --> 00:29:42.780
Oh, what do you know?

00:29:43.330 --> 00:29:44.490
The bridal suite.

00:29:44.690 --> 00:29:45.550
At last.

00:29:46.960 --> 00:29:49.720
I settled for a tent about a thousand miles from here.

00:29:49.980 --> 00:29:51.540
I know what you mean.

00:29:53.140 --> 00:29:55.600
Right now, even my desk at the home office would look good.

00:29:56.020 --> 00:29:57.360
Let's check the joint just in case.

00:29:57.720 --> 00:29:58.080
Good idea.

00:30:19.010 --> 00:30:25.760
Hey, this is swell layout.

00:30:26.300 --> 00:30:26.500
Yeah.

00:30:30.990 --> 00:30:38.930
Come on. What do you think?

00:30:39.780 --> 00:30:42.240
Afraid we haven't much choice. At least it's comfortable.

00:30:43.640 --> 00:30:46.660
You know, maybe it isn't as bad as we think. The Army must be doing something.

00:30:47.020 --> 00:30:51.260
Yeah, only in the meantime, we've got to play hide-and-seek with a bunch of zombies for Mars or wherever they come from.

00:30:51.360 --> 00:30:54.200
He's right, Frank. They're bound to find out where we are sooner or later.

00:30:54.820 --> 00:30:59.700
No. I'm about the only thing we can do is wait till it's dark and then try to sneak out of town toward the south.

00:31:01.050 --> 00:31:02.410
Forgetting what happened to Otis, I...

00:31:04.640 --> 00:31:05.480
Forgetting a thing.

00:31:39.850 --> 00:31:50.020
fine tell you the situation is critical roughly 2300 last night when their first units landed here

00:31:50.020 --> 00:31:58.150
in sector b-97 they have been confronted with an enemy the like of which defies description who

00:31:58.430 --> 00:31:59.350
what they are

00:32:00.320 --> 00:32:01.160
It's an open question.

00:32:03.930 --> 00:32:05.170
This is till we take a few prisoners.

00:32:05.690 --> 00:32:06.930
So far, we haven't been able to do that.

00:32:08.890 --> 00:32:10.010
What we can be sure of is this.

00:32:11.500 --> 00:32:15.060
The invasion was not launched by any power on the surface of this Earth.

00:32:18.910 --> 00:32:20.110
What about the scientists, General?

00:32:20.920 --> 00:32:23.360
Haven't they any idea where the enemy could have originated?

00:32:24.240 --> 00:32:27.000
The consensus of theories points to the planet Venus.

00:32:28.100 --> 00:32:29.980
Assuming, of course, that the invaders are human.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:36.650
beings like ourselves is there any reason to believe they're not frankly we don't know what

00:32:36.650 --> 00:32:42.280
to think what fragmentary reports we've been able to piece together indicate they behave like

00:32:42.280 --> 00:32:49.460
automatons apparently completely indifferent to personal danger they've made no effort to break

00:32:49.460 --> 00:32:57.820
out of the city but it's only a matter of how many of them several hundred at most

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:02.000
Only an advanced element for the main force.

00:33:02.990 --> 00:33:05.030
A few hundred men shouldn't be much of a problem.

00:33:05.830 --> 00:33:06.650
That's what we thought.

00:33:06.830 --> 00:33:11.240
The first contact was made by the 387th Airborne.

00:33:12.240 --> 00:33:16.360
And about 2400, they were up to a man.

00:33:16.460 --> 00:33:25.880
In a moment, our main line fence is here in the semicircle,

00:33:26.060 --> 00:33:27.980
roughly 10 miles south of the city line.

00:33:28.600 --> 00:33:29.980
Third Armored is holding down the...

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:32.540
Left here, 7th is on the right.

00:33:33.460 --> 00:33:35.080
They're both pretty much chewed up by now.

00:33:36.560 --> 00:33:37.180
General Wood, sir.

00:33:37.410 --> 00:33:37.810
What is it?

00:33:38.050 --> 00:33:40.190
Airstrike in progress against the main enemy position.

00:33:40.480 --> 00:33:42.080
Colonel Meade thought you'd want to follow it by radar.

00:35:00.730 --> 00:35:01.390
Are they always?

00:35:01.610 --> 00:35:02.860
I think so.

00:35:03.300 --> 00:35:04.580
Then they're going to bomb the city.

00:35:04.840 --> 00:35:07.160
Just keep your fingers crossed that we're not in the middle of the target.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:02.140
We must have weapons we've never even dreamed of.

00:36:02.670 --> 00:36:03.390
Well, that figures.

00:36:03.790 --> 00:36:05.810
They were smart enough to get here in the first place.

00:36:11.460 --> 00:36:12.400
Who are they, Frank?

00:36:13.060 --> 00:36:14.300
Where can they come from?

00:36:14.540 --> 00:36:15.300
Who can tell?

00:36:16.040 --> 00:36:17.260
My guess would be Venus.

00:36:17.640 --> 00:36:18.500
What makes you say that?

00:36:19.380 --> 00:36:21.300
As far as I know, it's the only planet

00:36:21.300 --> 00:36:23.380
that might be capable of supporting human life.

00:36:23.980 --> 00:36:25.880
It's covered by a heavy layer of clouds.

00:36:26.060 --> 00:36:28.580
That means plenty of water, oxygen, and hydrogen

00:36:28.580 --> 00:36:29.420
in its atmosphere.

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:31.100
Say, where'd you learn all this?

00:36:31.540 --> 00:36:31.900
College.

00:36:33.240 --> 00:36:34.780
I mean, I didn't get it all from the classrooms.

00:36:35.480 --> 00:36:38.480
I had a buddy named Richard Banks, a regular science fiction bug.

00:36:38.660 --> 00:36:40.260
He got me reading the magazines, too.

00:36:40.630 --> 00:36:42.050
Don't tell me you believe all that stuff.

00:36:42.230 --> 00:36:45.350
Oh, not all of it, but some of those writers weren't too far off the beam.

00:36:45.470 --> 00:36:47.150
There's plenty of evidence of that right outside.

00:36:47.800 --> 00:36:52.620
Yeah, and if the Air Force couldn't get past those guys, it don't look too good for us.

00:36:53.730 --> 00:36:56.710
Those planes were shot down a good 15 miles south of here.

00:36:57.010 --> 00:36:58.830
That would mean the whole city must be surrounded.

00:36:59.530 --> 00:36:59.970
You mean even...

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:02.760
And if we did get out of here after dark, it wouldn't do any good.

00:37:03.000 --> 00:37:05.720
I'm afraid we wouldn't get any further than Otis did.

00:37:13.540 --> 00:37:15.440
Oh, you guys are a big help.

00:37:15.700 --> 00:37:17.820
If things aren't rough enough, you have to scare her half to death.

00:37:17.940 --> 00:37:19.160
Well, all I said was...

00:37:19.160 --> 00:37:20.220
Oh, skip it. Vicki's right.

00:37:20.570 --> 00:37:22.350
We did act like a couple of chumps.

00:37:36.400 --> 00:37:38.660
I'm sorry, Nora. I shouldn't have said that.

00:37:39.010 --> 00:37:40.680
Why not? Is the truth?

00:37:41.640 --> 00:37:43.840
We might still have a chance to get out of this.

00:37:44.100 --> 00:37:46.160
After all, we know the Air Force is still fighting.

00:37:46.300 --> 00:37:47.300
Only we're right in the middle.

00:37:49.450 --> 00:37:50.090
Funny, isn't it?

00:37:51.300 --> 00:37:55.040
Time yesterday, I wouldn't have cared if they dropped an H-bomb right on the roof.

00:37:58.730 --> 00:37:59.370
What do you mean?

00:38:01.340 --> 00:38:04.700
This afternoon when you found me, I told you I'd slept through the evacuation.

00:38:05.810 --> 00:38:08.550
Well, didn't that sound a little peculiar to you?

00:38:10.950 --> 00:38:14.000
Maybe I didn't think it was any of my business then.

00:38:16.290 --> 00:38:16.730
And now?

00:38:18.190 --> 00:38:19.530
A lot's happened since then.

00:38:20.430 --> 00:38:22.730
Now I want to know everything I can about you.

00:38:24.040 --> 00:38:27.900
Would it make any difference if I told you the reason I slept through everything was because...

00:38:28.690 --> 00:38:29.970
because I never intended...

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:43.930
to wake up at all i tried to kill myself last night frank sleeping pills i know what you're

00:38:43.930 --> 00:38:50.480
thinking otis wanted to live and he died i wanted to die and oh i guess it doesn't make much suicide

00:38:51.840 --> 00:38:59.460
never does but why should a girl like you what do you know about me i could be anything a thief a

00:38:59.460 --> 00:38:59.980
Murderers.

00:39:00.800 --> 00:39:01.500
Even worse.

00:39:01.850 --> 00:39:02.890
No, I don't think so.

00:39:03.880 --> 00:39:06.340
Whatever you did, there must have been a very good reason.

00:39:06.380 --> 00:39:08.180
You don't need a reason to die, Frank.

00:39:09.560 --> 00:39:10.480
Just one to live.

00:39:12.640 --> 00:39:14.640
How I thought that I didn't have one anymore.

00:39:17.050 --> 00:39:17.890
Still feel that way.

00:39:19.940 --> 00:39:22.230
I don't know why, but everything's changed.

00:39:24.370 --> 00:39:25.470
You'd like to do anything about it.

00:39:33.680 --> 00:39:36.720
Report from the 337th Fighter Bomber Command.

00:39:37.550 --> 00:39:38.330
Any of them get through?

00:39:40.150 --> 00:39:40.750
Out of one, sir.

00:39:44.120 --> 00:39:45.280
Jets can't get through nothing.

00:39:45.580 --> 00:39:48.410
What about the atomic artillery?

00:39:49.360 --> 00:39:51.540
We got the new models that were flown in an hour ago.

00:39:51.720 --> 00:39:53.080
They won't be assembled for several hours.

00:39:54.490 --> 00:39:55.970
Are they sending us the new guided missiles?

00:39:56.700 --> 00:39:59.240
Yes, we receive those along with the atomic artillery.

00:40:00.380 --> 00:40:03.760
I never thought the day would come when we turned them against one of our own cities.

00:40:05.260 --> 00:40:06.680
There won't be a building left standing.

00:40:07.170 --> 00:40:08.250
I know, I know.

00:40:08.960 --> 00:40:09.620
Can't be helped.

00:40:13.690 --> 00:40:16.050
It's in dispatch, sir, from Colonel Powers, 7th Army Division.

00:40:20.430 --> 00:40:20.970
Captured one.

00:40:21.920 --> 00:40:22.460
How'd they do it?

00:40:22.980 --> 00:40:26.540
Tank crew picked them up by the side of the road in sector B-107.

00:40:27.360 --> 00:40:29.900
Says it was completely inactive, lying.

00:40:31.530 --> 00:40:31.990
Where is he now?

00:40:32.310 --> 00:40:33.750
They're bringing him into the lab, sir.

00:40:34.250 --> 00:40:34.810
The lab?

00:40:35.410 --> 00:40:36.390
Why not to interrogation?

00:40:37.240 --> 00:40:38.900
We'll find out when we get over there.

00:40:39.000 --> 00:40:39.300
Come on.

00:40:45.980 --> 00:40:47.680
That's a third pair in the last 10 minutes.

00:40:48.840 --> 00:40:49.880
I wonder where they're going.

00:40:50.310 --> 00:40:50.870
I don't know.

00:40:51.240 --> 00:40:53.040
But I got a good suggestion for them.

00:40:54.180 --> 00:40:56.500
Vicki, how can you joke at a time like this?

00:40:56.660 --> 00:40:57.920
Don't kid yourself, honey.

00:40:58.020 --> 00:40:59.960
The only reason I open my trap is to keep...

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:04.460
my teeth from chattering. Those things out there are bad enough in broad daylight. It's going to be

00:41:04.460 --> 00:41:08.630
dark pretty soon. You know, I was just thinking, as long as we have to stay here,

00:41:09.010 --> 00:41:12.730
we might as well do it the right way. Now, there must be a flashlight or some candles around

00:41:12.730 --> 00:41:17.150
somewhere. Why don't I go and look for them? Can you go downstairs alone? With all those creeps

00:41:17.150 --> 00:41:21.010
around, not on your life. Well, we have to have some light, and who knows, I might be able to find

00:41:21.010 --> 00:41:26.390
some food. All right, but I'm going with you. One of us ought to stay here with the girls. All right,

00:41:26.470 --> 00:41:29.730
you stay. Oh, we're so gallant all of a sudden. Yesterday,

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:32.140
He wouldn't even stand up to give me a seat on the bus.

00:41:32.460 --> 00:41:34.880
Yeah, and today the buses aren't running anymore.

00:41:35.630 --> 00:41:38.790
Jim is right, Frank. You should both go. It's the only fair thing to do.

00:41:38.910 --> 00:41:39.830
Yeah, but what about you and Vicki?

00:41:39.910 --> 00:41:43.630
Don't worry about us. We'll lock yourselves in till you get back.

00:41:44.180 --> 00:41:45.740
Come on, get started while I stir some light.

00:41:46.370 --> 00:41:46.610
Come on.

00:42:06.300 --> 00:42:06.680
Right here, sir.

00:42:07.240 --> 00:42:07.700
Hi, Tom.

00:42:08.040 --> 00:42:08.560
Hello, General.

00:42:14.100 --> 00:42:14.400
Yes, sir.

00:42:14.540 --> 00:42:15.740
We think they all are.

00:42:17.300 --> 00:42:17.620
Fantastic.

00:42:19.120 --> 00:42:20.900
No wonder we haven't been able to stop them anywhere.

00:42:21.670 --> 00:42:23.870
Well, at least now we know what we're up against.

00:42:24.960 --> 00:42:26.940
We only had a little time to work out a defense.

00:42:27.180 --> 00:42:28.940
Well, we've already started electronic research.

00:42:29.510 --> 00:42:29.970
The objective...

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:36.090
to being to find out what caused this break we might have a few hours if we're lucky and they

00:42:36.090 --> 00:42:42.270
hold off reinforcing their advance elements the general staff been notified yes sir major reynolds

00:42:42.270 --> 00:42:48.750
sent an urgent message good they'll probably want to fly in the team from g2 what are the landing

00:42:48.750 --> 00:42:59.970
strip enable sector held at all costs yes sir take almost four hours doubt the

00:43:00.690 --> 00:43:05.660
I understand, General. We'll do everything we can, just in case.

00:43:53.800 --> 00:43:59.510
away from the window norah no use taking any more chances than we have sorry i guess i wasn't thinking

00:44:00.220 --> 00:44:01.560
We shouldn't have let them go, Vicki.

00:44:02.280 --> 00:44:03.980
Something's gone wrong, I know it.

00:44:06.230 --> 00:44:07.490
Hey, take it easy, kid.

00:44:07.850 --> 00:44:09.250
They've been gone almost 20 minutes.

00:44:09.570 --> 00:44:13.730
If anything's happened to Frank, I'll never forgive myself.

00:44:14.480 --> 00:44:16.200
I thought you just met him today.

00:44:16.480 --> 00:44:17.900
What's that got to do with it?

00:44:18.260 --> 00:44:19.910
Nothing, not a thing.

00:44:21.160 --> 00:44:22.540
It's just that way with me and Jim.

00:44:23.330 --> 00:44:25.070
Only neither one of us was smart enough

00:44:25.070 --> 00:44:26.130
to do anything about it.

00:44:28.630 --> 00:44:29.890
Hey, open up, it's us.

00:44:34.570 --> 00:44:35.570
I bet you'd never get that.

00:44:35.710 --> 00:44:37.230
Hey, you hit the jackpot!

00:44:37.430 --> 00:44:38.450
You ain't seen nothing yet.

00:44:38.630 --> 00:44:40.670
Better wait till I make sure the drapes are drawn tightly.

00:44:40.930 --> 00:44:41.230
Okay.

00:44:51.380 --> 00:44:52.700
Yeah, all the comforts of home.

00:44:52.950 --> 00:44:54.570
Sure, if you like haunted houses.

00:44:55.490 --> 00:44:57.970
Don't you two ever do anything besides insult each other?

00:44:58.110 --> 00:44:59.170
Oh, we have our moments.

00:44:59.410 --> 00:44:59.590
Yeah.

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:00.780
But this isn't one of them.

00:45:01.050 --> 00:45:01.970
Oh, funny.

00:45:02.490 --> 00:45:04.130
How long do you think we'll have to stay here?

00:45:04.690 --> 00:45:06.290
I'm afraid that's up to the army.

00:45:07.640 --> 00:45:08.500
Yeah, but whose?

00:45:09.130 --> 00:45:10.110
Ours or theirs?

00:45:26.710 --> 00:45:27.170
Don't do that.

00:45:27.730 --> 00:45:29.890
You'd think you were in a cage or something the way you keep pacing around.

00:45:30.570 --> 00:45:31.710
What do you want me to do?

00:45:32.040 --> 00:45:33.780
Take a nice long walk out in the street,

00:45:34.620 --> 00:45:36.140
a few more hours in this flea trap,

00:45:36.140 --> 00:45:37.440
and we'll all be stir-crazy.

00:45:37.660 --> 00:45:38.800
Well, at least we're still alive.

00:45:39.060 --> 00:45:40.280
Now sit down and keep your mouth shut.

00:45:40.440 --> 00:45:41.520
Who do you think you are,

00:45:41.580 --> 00:45:43.200
ordering me around like a train monkey?

00:45:43.840 --> 00:45:45.260
You think we were married or something?

00:45:45.440 --> 00:45:45.960
Well, if we're not,

00:45:46.040 --> 00:45:47.040
it ain't because you haven't been trying

00:45:47.040 --> 00:45:48.040
for the last ten years.

00:45:48.460 --> 00:45:50.150
Go ahead. Rub it in.

00:45:50.610 --> 00:45:52.290
I ought to have my head examined

00:45:52.290 --> 00:45:53.570
for putting up with you at all.

00:45:54.050 --> 00:45:54.990
We wouldn't be here now

00:45:54.990 --> 00:45:56.170
if you listened to me last night.

00:45:56.330 --> 00:45:57.810
Sure, the whole thing's my fault.

00:45:57.870 --> 00:45:59.070
I even planned the invasion.

00:45:59.550 --> 00:45:59.970
We still...

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:01.740
You still could have been evacuated with the others.

00:46:02.230 --> 00:46:05.480
No. No, you had to drink your way through half the bars in town.

00:46:05.620 --> 00:46:07.180
All right, so I did a little celebrating.

00:46:07.520 --> 00:46:09.880
How often does a guy hit the daily double at 60 to 1?

00:46:10.560 --> 00:46:12.900
Once in 10 years, if you're any example.

00:46:13.760 --> 00:46:17.540
Let's live, baby. I hit the GGs for 240 clams.

00:46:17.820 --> 00:46:20.060
Ha! Lotta good the money is now.

00:46:20.300 --> 00:46:22.760
You didn't have to come along. You ain't the only blonde around.

00:46:30.890 --> 00:46:48.220
Jim, why do we have to fight like this all the time?

00:47:13.150 --> 00:47:13.950
Firework's over.

00:47:14.130 --> 00:47:17.070
For a few rounds, anyway.

00:47:18.780 --> 00:47:20.060
You know, it's funny about those two.

00:47:20.480 --> 00:47:22.340
Gee, they needle each other every minute.

00:47:22.780 --> 00:47:23.840
Yep, when the chips are down.

00:47:24.040 --> 00:47:24.380
I know.

00:47:25.470 --> 00:47:27.030
Jerry and I were a lot like that.

00:47:28.590 --> 00:47:28.910
Jerry?

00:47:30.510 --> 00:47:39.220
My husband, thanks.

00:47:42.950 --> 00:47:44.620
What happened to your husband?

00:47:46.220 --> 00:47:50.270
Killed in an automobile accident six months ago.

00:47:51.860 --> 00:47:53.780
Oh, we were arguing just like Jim and Vicky.

00:47:54.110 --> 00:47:56.530
I was driving, never even saw the car that hit us.

00:47:57.580 --> 00:47:59.860
When I regained consciousness in the hospital, they...

00:48:01.020 --> 00:48:02.340
They call me germs.

00:48:06.100 --> 00:48:07.860
You've been blaming yourself ever since.

00:48:10.200 --> 00:48:12.080
Is that why you took those sleeping pills?

00:48:13.840 --> 00:48:14.020
Yes.

00:48:17.470 --> 00:48:21.150
Fiona, but you can't keep on letting it get you like I did last night.

00:48:21.820 --> 00:48:22.600
I'm sorry.

00:48:24.290 --> 00:48:26.390
It's just that I've never been able to talk about it.

00:48:28.280 --> 00:48:28.440
Oh.

00:48:30.990 --> 00:48:33.030
We've been on the go for nearly 14 hours.

00:48:33.490 --> 00:48:34.650
What you need is a little sleep.

00:48:36.070 --> 00:48:37.990
With one of those things or whatever they are,

00:48:38.130 --> 00:48:39.830
I would have burst in here any minute.

